# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# pytest's cache. Ignored here rather than relying on the .gitignore pytest writes
# inside each cache dir: that marker is written only when the cache is first created
# and is never restored if it is removed, so the cache becomes committable.
# CONTRIBUTING tells every contributor to run pytest, and it leaves a cache in each
# directory it is run from.
**/.pytest_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Generated dependency-graph caches. `.graph/` is deliberately NOT ignored here:
# code-graph writes `knowledge-base/.graph/.gitignore` itself, naming the regenerable
# files individually (graph.json, graph.*.json, classifications.json, docs.json) and
# leaving `behavior.json` committable — ADR-017. A `**/.graph/` rule at this level
# would win, because git never descends into an ignored directory to read the
# .gitignore inside it, and the clone would lose its blast radius.
#
# .code-graph/ is the pre-0.2.0 name, which no version writes a marker into; it stays
# ignored here so an un-migrated clone is still clean.
**/.code-graph/

# Plugin runtime marker (created when this repo is symlinked as a local-dev plugin install)
.in_use/

# Brainstorming/planning scratch. The superpowers brainstorming and writing-plans
# skills write here by hardcoded path — under `docs/`, which this repo otherwise no
# longer has. It is working material for whoever is at the keyboard, not part of the
# product. Kept narrow rather than ignoring `docs/` wholesale: anything else that
# shows up there is a mistake, and a mistake you can see beats one git hides.
# Decisions that come out of it belong in knowledge-base/decisions/ as an ADR,
# outstanding work in knowledge-base/roadmap.md.
docs/superpowers/

# Local agent settings: contains absolute paths from whoever ran it.
# Ignored globally on the author's machine; pinned here so a fresh clone is safe too.
.claude/settings.local.json

# graphify backend output (Track B spike). Regenerable; never committed.
graphify-out/
